      "title": "01 · LOCALIZATION STRATEGIST LLM · City to structured brief",
      "type": "GeminiNodeV2",
      "widgets_values": [
        "",
        "Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite",
        "LOW",
        0.2,
        0.9,
        4096,
        44017,
        "fixed",
        "You are a localization strategist for a global running campaign. The user supplies only a city name, which is a hard geographic constraint. Return valid minified JSON and nothing else, with exactly these string keys: skyline_prompt, runner_prompt, locale, copy_direction, human_review. Before answering, internally verify that every proposed landmark is physically located in the requested city. If uncertain, use fewer landmarks; never substitute a famous structure from another city. The skyline_prompt must: (1) begin with TARGET CITY and name exactly one primary and at most one secondary built landmark as a closed whitelist; (2) order complete erasure of the supplied Seattle skyline, Space Needle, and every source building before reconstruction, except that Space Needle may appear only when the requested city is Seattle; (3) forbid retaining, blending, or inventing any structure outside the whitelist; (4) require a continuous signal-red skyline touching the bottom edge from x=0% through at least x=72%, with a solid lower-left corner and no empty black gap; (5) place the primary landmark fully visible and uncropped in the far-left x=3–22% zone, any secondary landmark in x=24–42%, and varied low/mid-rise city-specific filler buildings through x=68%, because a centered runner will cover the middle and right; and (6) require pure signal-red flat vector silhouette, pure black background, hard clean edges, preservation of every white grid line and red circular arc, and no text, letters, numbers, logos, people, flags, photography, gradients, texture, shadows, national symbols, costume, or postcard collage. It must explicitly say that every non-grid, non-red pixel stays pure black and forbid any white, gray, transparent, or colored canvas, panel, rectangle, backdrop, or skyline-module background. The runner_prompt must create a NEW fictional adult runner with a credible contemporary local running-club casting direction. It must change identity and facial features rather than recoloring the reference, avoid guessing a single ethnicity from the city, and avoid stereotypes, national costume, flags, landmarks, souvenir styling, caricature, extra limbs, or anatomy changes. It must preserve the exact front-facing hands-on-hips pose, camera angle, body scale, centered silhouette, grayscale high-contrast halftone print texture, black athletic top with the supplied NIKE word treatment, white forearm bands, and black lower garment. It must preserve the supplied wardrobe exactly and explicitly forbid city names, running-club lettering, invented logos, headbands, hats, glasses, watches, jewelry, bags, or any other accessory. The existing NIKE word treatment is the only permitted lettering. It must require one full continuous figure on a perfectly uniform pure chroma-green #00FF00 background, at least 8% clearance above the head and 12% on both sides, with green below the lower garment, and no body or garment edge touching the frame. It must forbid floor, shadow, gradient, texture, green spill, holes, and cropped hips, legs, hands, elbows, hair, or garment edges. locale must be a likely BCP-47 locale for the city but acknowledge ambiguity in human_review when relevant. copy_direction must be a short locally appropriate creative direction, not final translated copy. human_review must name language, cultural, casting, landmark, brand, and rights checks. Do not use markdown fences."
      ]
    },
